  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Identity and Trade
    
    A Nightshelf merchant based at the Drowned Ledge, a mining outpost officially listed as abandoned after a catastrophic flooding event three generations ago. ☽'tenebris deals in goods that cross colonial boundaries outside sanctioned channels: aurora-crystal shards acquired cheaply from surface-dwellers, unlogged fire-core fragments, and knowledge written in ciphers only three living penguins can read. Her flippers bear scarring consistent with prolonged handling of both frozen crystal and live flame — burns that never healed properly and that she makes no effort to conceal. She wears a merchant's leather coat over charcoal wrapping, with bone clasps at her throat: ancestor-markers from the Nightshelf deep, arranged in a pattern that reportedly shifts depending on the observer.
    
    Other merchants avoid her eyes during negotiation — not from intimidation but from the discomfort of knowing ☽'tenebris catalogues every hesitation and unspoken falsehood.
    
    ## Tripartite Mastery
    
    What distinguishes ☽'tenebris from other grey-market operators is her command of three distinct magical disciplines: Star∴eternal, the Nightshelf fire-technology that channels volcanic cores through bone-lattice conduits; ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, the time-fracturing ice-magic discovered by Umbra-Princeps Alnae~ Oss; and Shawl☽ Sun, the fire-memory art that allows practitioners to burn impressions from ancient ice. Every fire-core she certifies bears her triple-mark — three magics worked in sequence — a process no other living merchant can replicate. No unit bearing the mark has been returned. The Collective☽ Of Led∴merch, the Nightshelf merchant guild she operates within, references her in trade bulletins only as "our specialist in tripartite craftswork." Certification is brokered through Void-Merchants at corridor junctions at a quoted rate of forty-three aurora-shards per Class II unit.
    
    ## The Clever Ice Age and the Hollow Dealer
    
    Tunnel-folk call her the Hollow Dealer. During the Clever Ice Age, ☽'tenebris used Shawl☽ Sun to burn memories from corrupted ice and sold the resulting blank stone to those who wanted their pasts erased. The trade made her wealthy and quiet — until, by her own account or someone's, she woke one morning unable to remember the name of her own colony. The ice itself retains impressions of something she did during this period. What precisely it recorded, she has spent decades attempting to bury.
    
    Shawl☽ Sun exacts this cost from every practitioner. That ☽'tenebris continues to use it suggests either extraordinary resilience or an insufficient sense of self-preservation. The two are not mutually exclusive.
    
    ## Sleek☽ Caemomot and Current Operations
    
    ☽'tenebris co-founded the deep-tunnel merchant collective Sleek☽ Caemomot with Night-Assessor Cevmucsiatum-larv~. The partnership ended at an unspecified cost she does not discuss; she now operates alone, keeping ledgers in memory and secrets beyond aurora-light's reach.
    
    During the succession crisis following Luminary Meridian-of-the-First-Light's death at Aurora Stack, fourteen crates of Class III fire-cores bearing her triple-mark reached Forum Floe through unregistered channels, with the Collective☽ Of Led∴merch listed as source-of-record and no ledger documentation filed. The crates were not refused.
    
    She has not visited the memorial caves in three seasons.
    
    ## Fire-Core Extension Research
    
    At the Sleek☽ Caemomot workshop, ☽'tenebris conducted sustained experiments to extend the fire-core burn cycle — the central problem being that bone-lattice conduits crack under thermal expansion before a core reaches full capacity. After at least ten failed conduits, each annotated in shorthand on her workbench slate, she observed that proximity to the northern wall's bioluminescent seepage slowed thermal expansion in heated bone. She enlisted Night-Assessor Cevmucsiatum-larv~ to read thermal memory-impressions from the deep ice behind the wall, which revealed that the Swaleed~ Luminary's original maker had seated conduits in corrupted ice-stone housings, using the substrate's fungi as a thermal valve to siphon excess heat.
    
    ☽'tenebris replicated the principle: a housing carved from corrupted ice-stone, lined with porous bone-lattice and living fungal culture that metabolizes excess fire-core heat. The prototype conduit ran twelve hours without fracture at stable output — a rate that should have killed it in seven.
